IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lss-dates`
IMPORT `lss-core`

-- Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) -- THE INJURED PERSON'S SEAT: the person injured in a
-- motor vehicle accident who asks whether the Lifetime Support Scheme covers them, how to join it, what it pays for, and
-- how to challenge its decisions. Every question is asked as that person would ask it, from facts that person can state
-- (a person with lawful authority to act for them, such as a parent or guardian, may ask on their behalf: s 54). The
-- rules are in lss-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (version of 2 December 2019).
-- CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The injured person's questions`

§§ `Does the Scheme cover my injury (ss 5, 6, 24, 55)`
-- Situation: you were injured in a motor vehicle accident.

@export I was injured in a motor vehicle accident: does the South Australian Lifetime Support Scheme Act apply to my injury, even if the accident was my fault (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 5)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor vehicle accident in which you were injured (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)
      `I have been accepted into the Scheme under s 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an accident before 1 July 2014: whether the Lifetime Support Authority has accepted you into the Scheme under the "buy in" provision (s 6)
GIVETH AN `Application answer`
`Does the Act apply to my injury` MEANS
    `does the Act apply to the injury (s 5)` `the day of the accident` `I have been accepted into the Scheme under s 6`

@export Am I eligible to be a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme for people catastrophically injured in motor vehicle accidents in South Australia, and as a lifetime or an interim participant (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 5, 24, 55)?
GIVEN `I am covered by an agreement with my workers compensation authority under s 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a work injury and are the subject of an agreement between the Lifetime Support Authority and ReturnToWorkSA (the WorkCover Corporation) or your self-insured employer under s 55 of the Act
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor vehicle accident (ISO 8601)
      `I have applied under s 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an accident before 1 July 2014: whether you have applied to buy in to the Scheme under s 6
      `I suffered a bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a bodily injury
      `it was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by, or arose out of, the use of a motor vehicle
      `the accident happened in South Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in South Australia
      `I was taking part in a road race` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured as a participant in a road race
      `it is also a work injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is also a work injury under the Return to Work Act 2014 (for example, you were injured driving for work)
      `the criteria` IS A `Rules criteria` @desc Which of the LSS Rules' eligibility criteria your injury meets (for example the criteria for a spinal cord injury, brain injury, amputation, burns or blindness): the criteria for lifetime participation, the criteria for interim participation only, or neither
      `I have been awarded damages for my future care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court judgment that is final, or a binding settlement, has awarded you damages for your future treatment, care and support needs for this injury
GIVETH AN `Eligibility answer`
`Am I eligible to be a participant in the Scheme` MEANS
    `is the person eligible (s 24)` `I am covered by an agreement with my workers compensation authority under s 55` `the day of the accident` `I have applied under s 6` `I suffered a bodily injury` `it was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle` `the accident happened in South Australia` `I was taking part in a road race` `it is also a work injury` `the criteria` `I have been awarded damages for my future care`

@export I was injured in a motor vehicle accident before 1 July 2014: can I buy in to the Lifetime Support Scheme as a lifetime participant (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 6)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor vehicle accident (ISO 8601)
      `who applies` IS AN `Applicant` @desc Who is making the application: you; a person with lawful authority to act for you (such as a guardian or an attorney); an insurer of a vehicle involved in the accident; the nominal defendant; or someone else
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application has been made to the Lifetime Support Authority, in the manner and form it determines
      `I have given the information required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Authority the information it requires to assess the application
      `the Authority has decided to accept me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has determined that it will accept you into the Scheme under s 6
      `I have paid the contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the Authority the contribution it determined (the amount needed to fund your lifetime care)
GIVETH A `Buy-in answer`
`Can I buy in to the Scheme for an injury before 1 July 2014` MEANS
    `can the person buy in (s 6)` `the day of the accident` `who applies` `I have applied` `I have given the information required` `the Authority has decided to accept me` `I have paid the contribution`

§§ `Applying to join the Scheme (ss 25, 26(10), 26(11))`

@export Can this person or body apply for me to become a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme, and do they need my consent (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 6(3), 25(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor vehicle accident (ISO 8601)
      `who applies` IS AN `Applicant` @desc Who wants to apply: you; a person with lawful authority to act for you (such as a guardian, an attorney, or a parent of a child); an insurer of a vehicle involved in the accident; the nominal defendant; or someone else (for example a relative without legal authority, or a hospital)
GIVETH A `Who may apply answer`
`Can this person apply for me to join the Scheme` MEANS
    `may this applicant apply (ss 25, 6)` `the day of the accident` `who applies`

@export By when does the Act guarantee that I can apply to join the Lifetime Support Scheme (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 25(7): the LSS Rules must allow at least 3 years from the accident; s 26(10): any interim participation is added for an application to become a lifetime participant)?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor vehicle accident (ISO 8601)
      `I have been an interim participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been an interim participant in the Scheme and are now applying to become a lifetime participant
      `the first day of my interim participation` IS A DATE @desc The first day you were an interim participant (any date if none)
      `the last day of my interim participation` IS A DATE @desc The last day you were an interim participant, or today if you still are (any date if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when does the Act guarantee I can apply to join the Scheme` MEANS
    `the last day the Act guarantees for applying (ss 25(7), 26(10))` `the day of the accident` `the interim days`
    WHERE
        `the interim days` MEANS
            IF `I have been an interim participant`
            THEN `the days of the period from` `the first day of my interim participation` `to` `the last day of my interim participation`
            ELSE 0

@export Is my application to join the Lifetime Support Scheme within the time the Act guarantees (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 25(6), (7), 26(10))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor vehicle accident (ISO 8601)
      `I have been an interim participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been an interim participant in the Scheme and are now applying to become a lifetime participant
      `the first day of my interim participation` IS A DATE @desc The first day you were an interim participant (any date if none)
      `the last day of my interim participation` IS A DATE @desc The last day you were an interim participant, or today if you still are (any date if none)
      `the day of my application` IS A DATE @desc The day the application was or will be made (ISO 8601)
GIVETH AN `Application period answer`
`Is my application within the time the Act guarantees` MEANS
    `is the application within the period the Act guarantees (ss 25(7), 26(10))` `the day of the accident` `the interim days` `the day of my application`
    WHERE
        `the interim days` MEANS
            IF `I have been an interim participant`
            THEN `the days of the period from` `the first day of my interim participation` `to` `the last day of my interim participation`
            ELSE 0

@export I was an interim participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme: by when must I start my court action for damages, with my interim participation added to the usual 3 years (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 26(11), modifying s 36 of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936)?
GIVEN `the day my cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day your right to sue for damages arose; for a road injury, usually the day of the accident (ISO 8601)
      `the first day of my interim participation` IS A DATE @desc The first day you were an interim participant
      `the last day of my interim participation` IS A DATE @desc The last day you were an interim participant, or today if you still are
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I start my damages action, with my interim participation added` MEANS
    `the last day of the extended limitation period (s 26(11))` `the day my cause of action accrued` (`the days of the period from` `the first day of my interim participation` `to` `the last day of my interim participation`)

§§ `Becoming a participant (s 26)`
-- Situation: you, or someone for you, have applied to join the Scheme.

@export Must the Lifetime Support Authority accept me as a participant in the Scheme, and as a lifetime or an interim participant (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 26(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied I am eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Lifetime Support Authority is satisfied that you are eligible to be a participant
      `my eligibility` IS A `Participation kind` @desc Which kind of participation you are eligible for under the LSS Rules' criteria: lifetime participation or interim participation
      `the Authority is satisfied the application was duly made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority is satisfied that the application for you to be a participant was properly made (in the manner and form it determines, with the information it requires)
GIVETH AN `Acceptance answer`
`Must the Authority accept me as a participant` MEANS
    `must the Authority accept the person (s 26(1) to (3))` `the Authority is satisfied I am eligible` `my eligibility` `the Authority is satisfied the application was duly made`

@export I am, or was, an interim participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme: must I be accepted as a lifetime participant (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 26(4) to (9))?
GIVEN `my status` IS A `Participation status` @desc Where you stand now: a lifetime participant; an interim participant; or a person whose interim participation has ended under the LSS Rules
      `the Authority is satisfied I am eligible for lifetime participation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has become satisfied that you are eligible for lifetime participation (usually decided after your injury has stabilised)
GIVETH A `Lifetime answer`
`Must I be accepted as a lifetime participant` MEANS
    `must the person be accepted as a lifetime participant (s 26(4))` `my status` `the Authority is satisfied I am eligible for lifetime participation`

§§ `What the Scheme pays for (ss 4, 27, 28, 39 to 41)`
-- Situation: you are a participant in the Scheme.

@export I am a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme: will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care, support or service (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 4, 27, 28)?
GIVEN `I am a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a participant in the Scheme (lifetime or interim) when the expense was incurred
      `my participation is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your participation in the Scheme was suspended when it was provided (for example while you are absent from Australia, or for not cooperating with an assessment)
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of need` @desc The kind of treatment, care or support: medical treatment (including pharmaceuticals); dental treatment; rehabilitation; ambulance transportation; respite care; attendant care and support services; aids and appliances; prostheses; education and vocational training; home and transport modification; workplace modification; another kind the Authority has determined to be covered, generally or for you; or another kind
      `the LSS Rules declare it excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the LSS Rules declare it to be an excluded treatment, care and support need
      `the Authority assessed it as one of my needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority's assessment of your treatment, care and support needs (or a review of it) includes it as necessary and reasonable and related to your injury
      `the LSS Rules exclude it from payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the LSS Rules exclude it from the Authority's liability to pay (s 27(3)(c))
      `the expense is necessary and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the expense itself is necessary and reasonable
      `it was provided free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was provided to you gratuitously: you have not paid for it and are not liable to pay for it (for example care given free by a relative)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when it was provided
      `it is an ordinary cost of raising a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a child: whether it would ordinarily fall within the ordinary costs of raising a child (care, upbringing, education and advancement), apart from costs reasonably incurred because of the injury
      `it must be provided by an approved provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the LSS Rules require it to be provided by an approved provider
      `the provider was approved at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider was an approved provider when it was provided
      `the provider is a medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was provided by a registered medical practitioner (a doctor)
      `the LSS Rules allowed the provider to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider acted in circumstances the LSS Rules allow
      `it was provided against the LSS Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was provided in contravention of the LSS Rules
      `it is within the LSS Rules' limits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is within any monetary or other limit the LSS Rules place on it
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`Will the Scheme pay for this treatment, care or support` MEANS
    `will the Authority pay (ss 4, 27, 28)` `I am a participant` `my participation is suspended` `the kind` `the LSS Rules declare it excluded` `the Authority assessed it as one of my needs` `the LSS Rules exclude it from payment` `the expense is necessary and reasonable` `it was provided free` `my age` `it is an ordinary cost of raising a child` `it must be provided by an approved provider` `the provider was approved at the time` `the provider is a medical practitioner` `the LSS Rules allowed the provider to act` `it was provided against the LSS Rules` `it is within the LSS Rules' limits`

@export I am a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme: at what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment or service (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 39 to 41)?
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Kind of service` @desc The treatment or service: treatment at a public hospital; conveying by ambulance; medical, dental or rehabilitation treatment elsewhere than at a public hospital; attendant care and support services; treatment at a private hospital; a service the Minister has identified for s 41 by notice in the Gazette; or another service
      `it is paid under a bulk billing arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority pays for it under a bulk billing arrangement with the Minister for Health or the provider
      `a maximum fee has been fixed for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has fixed a maximum fee for it by notice in the Gazette under s 41
GIVETH A `Rate answer`
`At what rate does the Authority pay for this treatment` MEANS
    `at what rate does the Authority pay (ss 39 to 41)` `the service` `it is paid under a bulk billing arrangement` `a maximum fee has been fixed for it`

§§ `My needs assessment (ss 30 to 32)`
-- Situation: the Authority is assessing your treatment, care and support needs.

@export The Lifetime Support Authority, or its assessor, has asked me to do something for the assessment of my needs (for example to undergo a medical examination): must I comply (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 31, 32(2)(e))?
GIVEN `I am a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a participant in the Scheme
      `the request is for my needs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request was made by the Authority or an assessor in connection with an assessment of your treatment, care and support needs
      `the request is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request is reasonable
GIVETH A `Cooperation answer`
`Must I comply with this request for my needs assessment` MEANS
    `must the participant comply with the request (s 31)` `I am a participant` `the request is for my needs assessment` `the request is reasonable`

§§ `Challenging a decision (Part 5)`
-- Situation: you disagree with a decision of the Lifetime Support Authority.

@export I disagree with a decision of the Lifetime Support Authority: how can I challenge it (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 33 to 38)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision` @desc What the decision is about: whether you suffered a bodily injury; whether the incident was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle; whether the accident occurred in South Australia; whether coverage is excluded because of a road race or a work injury; whether your application was made in time under the LSS Rules; a determination suspending your participation; whether your injury resulted from the accident or from something else; whether your injury satisfies the LSS Rules' eligibility criteria; how two or more of your injuries are related; whether your injury is within or excluded from coverage under the LSS Rules; the assessment of your treatment, care and support needs; or another decision
      `I am a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a participant in the Scheme
GIVETH A `Review route answer`
`How can I challenge this decision` MEANS
    `which review is open (Part 5)` `the decision` `I am a participant`

@export Will the Lifetime Support Authority pay this cost of my review or dispute (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 34(9), (10), 36(5), (6), 38(10), (11))?
GIVEN `the forum` IS A `Forum` @desc Where the review is: before a review officer (s 34); an expert review panel on an eligibility dispute (s 36); an expert review panel reviewing your needs assessment (s 38); or the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal
      `the cost` IS A `Cost` @desc The cost: your travel and accommodation to attend; the travel and accommodation of a carer (who may be a parent) who accompanies and supports you; the cost of being represented (for example by a lawyer); or another cost of the proceedings
      `the cost is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For travel and accommodation: whether the cost is necessary for attending
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
`Will the Authority pay this cost of my review` MEANS
    `does the Authority pay this cost (ss 34, 36, 38)` `the forum` `the cost` `the cost is necessary`

@export By when must I apply to the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal for review of a review officer's or expert review panel's determination (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 35(2), 37(3): within 28 days of the date of the determination)?
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The date of the review officer's or expert review panel's determination (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to the Tribunal` MEANS
    `the last day to apply to the Tribunal (ss 35(2), 37(3))` `the day of the determination`

@export Can I apply, or did I apply in time, to the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal for review of a review officer's or expert review panel's determination (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 35, 37)?
GIVEN `the route` IS A `Tribunal route` @desc Which determination you want reviewed: a review officer's determination (s 35), or an expert review panel's determination that you are ineligible or do not qualify for the Scheme (s 37)
      `I am a party to the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a review officer's determination: whether you were a party to the dispute before the review officer (the person it was about is one)
      `the day of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The date of the determination (ISO 8601)
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to the Tribunal
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied (any date if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Tribunal answer`
`Am I in time to apply to the Tribunal` MEANS
    `may the person apply to the Tribunal (ss 35, 37)` `the route` `I am a party to the dispute` `the day of the determination` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today`

@export By when must I apply for an expert review panel to review the assessment of my treatment, care and support needs (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 38(3): within 28 days after I am given notice of it, unless the LSS Rules allow more time)?
GIVEN `the day I was given notice of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of the assessment (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for review of my needs assessment` MEANS
    `the last day to apply for review of the assessment (s 38(3))` `the day I was given notice of the assessment`

@export Can I apply, or did I apply in time, for an expert review panel to review the assessment of my treatment, care and support needs (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 38)?
GIVEN `I am a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a participant in the Scheme
      `the day I was given notice of the assessment` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of the assessment (ISO 8601)
      `an extension of time has been allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an extension of time has been allowed under the LSS Rules
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied for the review
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied (any date if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Assessment review answer`
`Am I in time to apply for review of my needs assessment` MEANS
    `may the participant apply for review of the assessment (s 38)` `I am a participant` `the day I was given notice of the assessment` `an extension of time has been allowed` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today`

§§ `Leaving Australia (s 52)`
-- Situation: you are a participant and plan to travel outside Australia.

@export I am a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme and plan to leave Australia: by when must I tell the Lifetime Support Authority (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 52(1): at least 28 days before leaving)?
GIVEN `the day I leave Australia` IS A DATE @desc The day you plan to leave Australia (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I tell the Authority I am leaving Australia` MEANS
    `the last day to give notice of the absence (s 52(1))` `the day I leave Australia`

@export I am a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme and plan to leave Australia: have I given, or can I still give, notice of my absence in time, and what can the Authority do (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 52)?
GIVEN `I am a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a participant in the Scheme
      `the day I leave Australia` IS A DATE @desc The day you plan to leave, or left, Australia (ISO 8601)
      `the Authority waived or reduced the notice period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has waived or reduced the 28-day notice period for you
      `I have given notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Authority notice of the proposed absence
      `the day I gave notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave notice (any date if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Absence answer`
`Have I given notice of my absence in time` MEANS
    `has the participant given notice of the absence in time (s 52)` `I am a participant` `the day I leave Australia` `the Authority waived or reduced the notice period` `I have given notice` `the day I gave notice` `today`

§§ `Offences (ss 34(6), 51)`

@export What is the most I can be fined under the Lifetime Support Scheme Act for this conduct (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) ss 34(6), 51)? The answer is the maximum penalty in dollars; 0 means this Act makes it no offence.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct` @desc What you did: gave information to the Authority (or another person acting under the Act); left information out of what you gave such a person; failed to appear, answer questions or produce material when a review officer required it; or something else
      `I knew it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For information given or left out: whether you knew that the information given was false or misleading
      `it was false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For information given or left out: whether it was false or misleading in a material (significant) respect
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a review officer's requirement: whether you had a reasonable excuse for not complying
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined` MEANS
    `the maximum penalty (ss 34(6), 51)` `the conduct` `I knew it was false or misleading` `it was false or misleading in a material particular` `I had a reasonable excuse`

§§ `Assessors, review officers and expert review panels (s 49, Schedule 1)`

@export Can I sue the Lifetime Support Scheme's assessor, review officer or expert review panel member personally for what they did or failed to do (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 49)?
GIVEN `they acted under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what they did or failed to do was in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act (for example assessing your needs or deciding your review)
      `they acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they acted, or failed to act, in good faith (honestly)
GIVETH AN `Immunity answer`
`Can I sue the assessor, review officer or panel member personally` MEANS
    `can the officer be sued personally (s 49)` `they acted under the Act` `they acted in good faith`

@export Can what I told an expert review panel be used in later proceedings (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) Schedule 1 cl 6(7))?
GIVEN `the proceedings are before a court or the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the later proceedings are before a court or the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal
      `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consent to the information being used
GIVETH A `Panel information answer`
`Can what I told the expert review panel be used in later proceedings` MEANS
    `can panel information be used in later proceedings (Sch 1 cl 6(7))` `the proceedings are before a court or the Tribunal` `I consent`
